I-generated summary\nL231: Google DeepMind introduces Nano Banana Pro, a new image generation and editing model built on Gemini 3 Pro. You can use it to create accurate visuals with legible text in multiple languages. Try Nano Banana Pro today across Google products like the Gemini app, Google Ads, and Google AI Studio.\nL232: \nL233: Summaries were generated by Google AI. Generative AI is experimental.\nL234:   * \"Introducing Nano Banana Pro\" is all about Google's new state-of-the-art image generation and editing model.\nL235:   * Nano Banana Pro helps you visualize ideas, create infographics, and turn notes into diagrams with ease.\nL236:   * Generate images with accurate text in multiple languages, perfect for mockups, posters, and international content.\nL237:   * Create high-fidelity visuals with consistent branding, advanced creative controls, and up to 4K resolution.\nL238:   * You can try Nano Banana Pro in Gemini, Google Ads, Workspace, and more, with SynthID watermarks for transparency.\nL239: Summaries were generated by Google AI. Generative AI is experimental.\nL240: #### Explore other styles:\nL241: \nL242:   * General summary\nL243:   * Bullet points\nL244: \nL245: Just a few months ago we released cite55†Nano Banana , our Gemini 2.5 Flash Image model. From cite56†restoring old photos†x.com to generating cite57†mini figurines†x.com , Nano Banana was a big step in image editing that empowered casual creators to express their creativity.\nL246: Today, we’re introducing cite58†Nano Banana Pro (Gemini 3 Pro Image)†deepmind.google , our new state-of-the art image generation and editing model. Built on cite59†Gemini 3 Pro , Nano Banana Pro uses Gemini’s state-of-the-art reasoning and real-world knowledge to visualize information better than ever before.\nL247: ## How Nano Banana Pro helps you bring any idea or design to life\nL248: \nL249: Nano Banana Pro can help you visualize any idea and design anything — from prototypes, to representing data as infographics, to turning handwritten notes into diagrams.\nL250: \nL251: With Nano Banana Pro, now you can:\nL252: \nL253: Generate more accurate, context-rich visuals based on enhanced reasoning, world knowledge and real-time information\nL254: With Gemini 3’s advanced reasoning, Nano Banana Pro doesn’t just create beautiful images, it also helps you create more helpful content. You can get accurate educational explainers to learn more about a new subject, like context-rich infographics and diagrams based on the content you provide or facts from the real world. Nano Banana Pro can also connect to Google Search's vast knowledge base to help you create a quick snapshot for a recipe or visualize real-time information like weather or sports.\nL255: cite60†Image: Infographic about plants using nano banana pro†storage.googleapis.com L256: \nL257: An infographic of the common house plant, String of Turtles, with information on origins, care essentials and growth patterns.\nL258: \nL259: Prompt: Create an infographic about this plant focusing on interesting information.\nL260: \nL261: cite61†Image: Infographic about making chai made using Nano Banana Pro†storage.googleapis.com L262: Step-by-step infographic for making Elaichi Chai (cardamom tea), demonstrating the ability to visualize recipes and real-world information.\nL263: \nL264: Prompt: Create an infographic that shows how to make elaichi chai\nL265: \nL266: cite62†Image: Comic book style weather infographic using Nano Banana Pro†storage.googleapis.com L267: \nL268: We used Nano Banana Pro to pull in real-time weather via Search grounding to build a pop-art infographic.\nL269: \nL270: Generate better visuals with more accurate, legible text directly in the image in multiple languages\nL271: Nano Banana Pro is the best model for creating images with correctly rendered and legible text directly in the image, whether you’re looking for a short tagline, or a long paragraph. Gemini 3 is great at understanding depth and nuance, which unlocks a world of possibilities with image editing and generation — especially with text. Now cite63†you can create more detailed text in mockups or posters with a wider variety of textures, fonts and calligraphy.\nL272: With Gemini’s enhanced multilingual reasoning, you can generate text in multiple languages, or localize and translate your content so you can scale internationally and/or share content more easily with friends and family.\nL273: cite64†Image: Storyboard showing four panels for \"Urban Astronaut\": establishing shot, medium shot, close-up, and POV shot up city buildings.†storage.googleapis.com L274: \nL275: A black and white storyboard sketch showing an establishing shot, medium shot, close-up, and POV shot for a film scene.\nL276: \nL277: Prompt: Create a storyboard for this scene\nL278: \nL279: cite65†Image: Berlin street view with facades spelling \"BERLIN\" in blue, red, white, and black block letters.†storage.googleapis.com L280: The word 'BERLIN' integrated into the architecture of a city block, spanning across multiple buildings.\nL281: \nL282: Prompt: View of a cozy street in Berlin on a bright sunny day, stark shadows. the old houses are oddly shaped like letters that spell out \"BERLIN\" Colored in Blue, Red, White and black. The houses still look like houses and the resemblance to letters is subtle.\nL283: \nL284: cite66†Image: Crash, whoosh, shiver, bang, drip, squeeze, roar, wobble in stylized fonts†storage.googleapis.com L285: Calligraphy inspired by meaning, showcasing the ability to generate expressive text with a wider variety of textures and fonts.\nL286: \nL287: Prompt: make 8 minimalistic logos, each is an expressive word, and make letters convey a message or sound visually to express the meaning of this word in a dramatic way. composition: flat vector rendering of all logos in black on a single white background\nL288: \nL289: cite67†Image: Cans in English and Korean†storage.googleapis.com L290: A beverage campaign concept showcasing accurate translation and rendering of English text into Korean.\nL291: \nL292: Prompt: translate all the English text on the three yellow and blue cans into Korean, while keeping everything else the same\nL293: \nL294: cite68†Image: The word \"TYPOGRAPHY\" in bold, stacked blue and magenta sans-serif text with a halftone/distressed effect.†storage.googleapis.com L295: \nL296: A graphic design featuring the word 'TYPOGRAPHY' with a retro, screen-printed texture.\nL297: Prompt: A vibrant, eye-catching \"TYPOGRAPHY\" design on a textured off-white background. The letters are bold, blocky, extra condensed and create a 3D effect with overlapping layers of bright blue and hot pink, each with a halftone dot pattern, evoking a retro print aesthetic. 16:9 aspect ratio\nL298: \nL299: cite69†Image: \"How much wood would a woodchuck chuck if a woodchuck could chuck wood\" made out of wood chucked by a woodchuck.†storage.googleapis.com L300: Blending text and texture in a creative way by integrating the phrase into a woodchopping scene.\nL301: \nL302: Prompt: Create an image showing the phrase \"How much wood would a woodchuck chuck if a woodchuck could chuck wood\" made out of wood chucked by a woodchuck.\nL303: \nL304: Create high-fidelity visuals with upgraded creative capabilities\nL305:   * Consistency by design: With Nano Banana Pro, you can blend more elements than ever before, using up to 14 images and maintaining the consistency and resemblance of up to 5 people. Whether turning sketches into products or blueprints into photorealistic 3D structures, you can now bridge the gap between concept and creation. Apply your desired visual look and feel to your mockups with ease, ensuring your branding remains seamless and consistent across every touchpoint.\nL306: cite70†Image: Fluffy characters watching TV†storage.googleapis.com L307: \nL308: Maintaining the consistency of up to 14 inputs, including multiple characters, across a complex composition.\nL309: Prompt: A medium shot of the 14 fluffy characters sitting squeezed together side-by-side on a worn beige fabric sofa and on the floor. They are all facing forwards, watching a vintage, wooden-boxed television set placed on a low wooden table in front of the sofa. The room is dimly lit, with warm light from a window on the left and the glow from the TV illuminating the creatures' faces and fluffy textures.\nL310: The background is a cozy, slightly cluttered living room with a braided rug, a bookshelf with old books, and rustic kitchen elements in the background. The overall atmosphere is warm, cozy, and amused.\nL311: cite71†Image: combining images of a gown, plants and a chair into one image†storage.googleapis.com L312: \nL313: Craft lifestyle scenes by combining multiple elements.\nL314: \nL315: Prompt: Combine these images into one appropriately arranged cinematic image in 16:9 format and change the dress on the mannequin to the dress in the image\nL316: \nL317: cite72†Image: generation of a futuristic sunset image†storage.googleapis.com L318: \nL319: Create surreal landscapes by combining multiple input elements.\nL320: Prompt: Combine these images into one appropriately arranged cinematic image in 16:9 format\nL321: \nL322: cite73†Image: Generated image of a fashion show from multiple elements†storage.googleapis.com L323: \nL324: A high-fashion editorial shot set in a desert landscape that maintains the consistency and resemblance of the people from the 6 input photos.\nL325: Prompt: Put these five people and this dog into a single image, they should fit into a stunning award-winning shot in the style if [sic] a fashion editorial. The identity of all five people and their attire and the dog must stay consistent throughout but they can and should be seen from different angles and distances in [sic] as is most natural and suitable to the scene. Make the colour and lighting look natural on them all, they look like they naturally fit into this fashion show.\nL326:   * Studio-quality creative controls: With Nano Banana Pro's new capabilities we are putting advanced creative controls directly into your hands. Select, refine and transform any part of an image with improved localized editing. Adjust camera angles, change the focus and apply sophisticated color grading, or even transform scene lighting (e.g. changing day to night or creating a bokeh effect).\nL327: Your creations are ready for any platform, from social media to print, thanks to a range of available aspect ratios and available 2K and 4K resolution\nL328: cite74†Image: changing the aspect ratio of an image using Nano Banana†storage.googleapis.com L329: \nL330: Change the look and feel of an image for a range of platforms by adapting the aspect ratio.\nL331: \nL332: Prompt: change aspect ratio to 1:1 by reducing background. The character, remains exactly locked in its current position\nL333: \nL334: cite75†Image: A fox in the snow in the daytime and at night†storage.googleapis.com L335: \nL336: Lighting and focus controls applied to transform a scene from day to night.\nL337: \nL338: Prompt: Turn this scene into nighttime\nL339: cite76†Image: Changing the lighting on a man's face to just show the eyes†storage.googleapis.com L340: \nL341: Obscure or enlighten a section of your image with lighting controls to achieve specific dramatic effects.\nL342: Prompt: Generate an image with an intense chiaroscuro effect. The man should retain his original features and expression. Introduce harsh, directional light, appearing to come from above and slightly to the left, casting deep, defined shadows across the face. Only slivers of light illuminating his eyes and cheekbones, the rest of the face is in deep shadow.\nL343: \nL344: cite77†Image: Changing the focus on an image from a woman in a flower field to the flowers in the foreground†storage.googleapis.com L345: Bring out the details of your composition by adjusting the depth of field or focal point (e.g., focusing on the flowers).\nL346: \nL347: Prompt: Focus on the flowers\nL348: ## How you can try Nano Banana Pro today\nL349: \nL350: Across our products and services, you now have a choice: the original Nano Banana for fast, fun editing, or Nano Banana Pro for complex compositions requiring the highest quality and visually sophisticated results.\nL351:   * Consumers and students: Rolling out globally in the cite78†Gemini app†gemini.google when you select ‘Create images’ with the ‘Thinking’ model. Our free-tier users will receive limited free quotas, after which they will revert to the original Nano Banana model. Google AI Plus, Pro and Ultra subscribers receive higher quotas. For AI Mode in Search, Nano Banana Pro is available in the U.S. for Google AI Pro and Ultra subscribers.\nL352: For cite79†NotebookLM†notebooklm.google , Nano Banana Pro is also available for subscribers globally.\nL353:   * Professionals: We're upgrading image generation in cite80†Google Ads†business.google.com to Nano Banana Pro to put cutting-edge creative and editing power directly into the hands of advertisers globally. It’s also rolling out starting today to cite81†Workspace customers†workspaceupdates.googleblog.com in cite82†Google Slides†slides.new and cite83†Vids†vids.new .\nL354:   * Developers and enterprise: Starting to roll out in the cite84†Gemini API and Google AI Studio , and in cite85†Google Antigravity†antigravity.google to create rich UX layouts & mockups; cite86†enterprises†cloud.google.com can start building in Vertex AI for scaled creation today and it’s coming soon to Gemini Enterprise.\nL355:   * Creatives: Starting to roll out to Google AI Ultra subscribers in cite87†Flow†flow.google , our AI filmmaking tool, to give creatives, filmmakers and marketers even more precision and control over their frames and scenes.\nL356: ## How to identify AI-generated images in the Gemini app\nL357: \n-------------------